# RUCHI — environment variables
# Copy to .env.local for local development.
#
# ── AI (server-side) ────────────────────────────────────────
# Google Gemini powers ingredient photo analysis. The key is used ONLY on
# the server inside the /api/analyze-ingredients route — it is never exposed
# to the browser. Get a key at https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
#
# ⚠ REQUIRED on Vercel: add GEMINI_API_KEY to
#   Project → Settings → Environment Variables → Production
# Without it the app stays fully usable except photo analysis, which shows
# a friendly unavailable message and falls back to manual ingredient entry.
GEMINI_API_KEY=your_gemini_api_key_here

# ── RUCHI accounts (Supabase Auth + Postgres) ───────────────
# Supabase owns user identity, profiles, completed meals and cooking
# streaks behind row-level security. It is never used for AI. Create a
# project at https://supabase.com, apply supabase/migrations/0001_ruchi_init.sql,
# then fill these in:
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR-PROJECT.supabase.co
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=your-publishable-anon-key
#
# ── Password reset ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Where reset-email links land. Must ALSO be allow-listed in the Supabase
# dashboard (Auth → URL Configuration → Redirect URLs). Leave unset for
# root deployments ("https://<origin>/" is used automatically); set it for
# non-root/preview deployments:
# NEXT_PUBLIC_PASSWORD_RESET_REDIRECT=https://YOUR-DOMAIN/
